d \"could not reproduce\" to both, so none are logged. I sent the bookmark report three times and each got that reply. I signed off at 0.4 confidence.\n\n**Where I saw problems:**\n- **Bookmarks and rotation:** A bookmark I added with \"Add to Bookmarks\" (Alpha) showed in the drawer, and still showed after I closed and reopened the drawer. After rotating to landscape it was gone, and it stayed gone back in portrait. I saw this three times. The built-in entries (DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures) stayed.\n- **Heading in the folder list:** With Directory Sort Mode \"None On Top\" and Sort By Last Modified descending, folder Alpha appeared last, under the \"Files\" heading. This may be normal behaviour for that mode, so I'm less sure about it.\n\n**What worked:**\n- **Rename:** The prompt is prefilled with the full name including the extension. Renaming a file and a folder both worked.\n- **Paste conflicts:** Choosing Rename produced \"readme (1).txt\", \"report+final (1).txt\" and \"Alpha (1)\". The copies had the right sizes and appeared in the right folder.\n- **Sorting:** Sorting by Name, Size, Type and Last Modified, and the \"Folders On Top\" and \"Files On Top\" modes, gave the expected order and headings. Grid view also looked fine.\n- **Bookmarks:** Adding a bookmark and deleting one through \"Modify Bookmark\" both worked.\n\n**Not tested:** cut/move paste, the Hidden Files option, and repeated pastes beyond the first \"(1)\" copy.\n\nI added and renamed a few things in AndroidQA/Amaze while testing: notes.txt is now notes2.txt, \"readme (1).txt\" is in Beta, \"report+final (1).txt\" is in Amaze, and a copy of Alpha is now Gamma.", "ttft_ms": 1949, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 317957, "uuid": "8ec27358-44d7-4c21-9b8e-7c4f48396f14", "ttft_stream_ms": 1891, "time_to_request_ms": 152, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 4, "system_prompt": 9, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 2, "input_attachments": 4, "input_hooks": 3, "conversation_append"